{
  "positions": [
    {
      "id": "joseki/4-4 point/Low approach",
      "stones": "B:pd W:nc",
      "toPlay": "B",
      "comments": [
        "{{White}} approaches the 4-4 stone with a small knight's move, the most common star point approach. {{Black}} answers by extending (small knight or one-space high), pincering, kicking, attaching, or playing elsewhere. Sources: 44PointLowApproach, 44PointLowApproachLowExtensionSlide33, 44PointLowApproachHighExtension, 44PointLowApproachAttach, 44PointOneSpaceLowPincerInvasionBlock.",
        "{{TR:O17|{{White}}'s low approach}} to {{TR:Q16|the 4-4 stone}}, along the top. The approach from the other side is the same position mirrored. Small knight approach (keima kakari). It threatens to slide into the corner at {{CR:Q18}} or to extend along the top, and it is the approach that strong players and AI programs prefer."
      ],
      "tags": {
        "name": [
          "4-4 point · low approach",
          "Small knight approach",
          "Keima kakari",
          "Kogeima kakari",
          "小ゲイマガカリ"
        ],
        "evaluation": 0,
        "status": "start",
        "topics": [
          "approach",
          "basic joseki"
        ],
        "difficulty": "20k",
        "sources": [
          "Sensei's Library (senseis.xmp.net), joseki pages listed in XSUM. Sequences copied from its diagrams and mirrored to the top-right corner."
        ],
        "era": [
          "classic",
          "modern",
          "ai"
        ]
      }
    },
